<title>NETHERLANDS: Lanschot sees Stork as Strong Outperformer.</title>
<headline>Lanschot sees Stork as Strong Outperformer.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Summary of March 6 research.</p>
<p>Company---------Sector--------Price---Broker----------------</p>
<p>Stork	     Engineering   81.40   Van Lanschot Bankiers</p>
<p>COMMENT: Strong Outperformer</p>
<p>Stork's '96 results exceeded expectations. After this transition year, company will fully benefit from contribution of subsidiary Fokker Aviation. In addition, several reorganised problem areas will be able to show substantial recovery. Outlook also good for longer term. Margins in most promising sector, industrial services, still low, but have scope for improvement. We think Stork will continue to outperform the market.  </p>
<p>    Estimates (NLG):  EPS     P/E    Dividend</p>
<p>    1996 (actual)     4.58    17.8   1.90</p>
<p>    1997		  5.55    14.7   2.25</p>
<p>    1998		  6.35    12.8   2.60</p>
